# Accepted "Dates differ" lines for orchard-replant.xml, one a line as the import report writes
# them. Each is a conversion the import report also lists, and a gap in ROADMAP.md (M4, import
# gaps). The percent lag (ID 4), As Late As Possible (ID 5) and the task after them (ID 6)
# match the file.

# Elapsed duration: ProjectCraft has no elapsed time, so 2ed becomes 2 working days; Project runs
# 48 hours round the clock, to Wednesday 08:00.
Dates differ: Start and finish (ID 2 Soak the rootstock): the file has 2026-10-05 to 2026-10-07; ProjectCraft works out 2026-10-05 to 2026-10-06

# Elapsed lag: 3ed becomes 3 working days, so the task starts a day later than after 72 hours
# round the clock (which end on the Saturday).
Dates differ: Start and finish (ID 3 Dig planting pits): the file has 2026-10-12 to 2026-10-13; ProjectCraft works out 2026-10-13 to 2026-10-14

# Task calendars aren't supported yet: the task is scheduled on the project calendar, on weekdays.
Dates differ: Start and finish (ID 7 Weekend watering): the file has 2026-10-10 to 2026-10-11; ProjectCraft works out 2026-10-08 to 2026-10-09

# A constraint is held to the day: Start No Earlier Than 13:00 starts at 08:00, so the task
# finishes the same day instead of the next morning.
Dates differ: Start and finish (ID 8 Mulch the rows): the file has 2026-10-14 to 2026-10-15; ProjectCraft works out 2026-10-14 to 2026-10-14

# Elapsed leveling delay: 2ed becomes 2 working days, Friday to Tuesday instead of to Monday.
Dates differ: Start and finish (ID 9 Prune the hedges): the file has 2026-10-12 to 2026-10-12; ProjectCraft works out 2026-10-13 to 2026-10-13
